//
// Phase E4 operator gate: elementwise_mul.
//
// The 2-D element-wise multiply the runlist mode's decomposed normalization
// needs for its gamma stage -- the one operator in the plan that existed
// nowhere in programming_examples/ before this phase. eltwise_add's streaming
// 2-D shape with vector_mul's arith.mulf; bf16 end to end, because the AIE
// vector unit does not legalize f32 vector element-wise multiply
// (weighted_rms_norm.py records the constraint).
//
// Two shapes: a cheap 512x512 first (the driver injects an operator's FIRST
// declared shape, so the standing negative control stays cheap), and 4096x768
// -- the exact tensor the runlist mode's two gamma multiplies dispatch. The
// second operand is drawn uniform(0.5, 1.5), the gamma-shaped range, which
// also bounds it away from zero at the injection site; see
// prepare_elementwise_mul.
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against an FP32 reference: np.isclose over the
// full output at rtol=1.6e-2, zero permitted mismatches. Measured atol_required
// is exactly 0.0 at both shapes -- a single bf16 rounding of an exact-in-f32
// product is always inside rtol alone.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipe below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// xclbin load and dispatch -- the same inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution and
// KernelCache take. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would
// DEADLOCK against the gate command that already holds it -- BSD flock(2)
// treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_elementwise_mul_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_elementwise_mul_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-elementwise-mul PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// Both lines, not just the verdict: the first is XRTRunner's own, the second
// names the operator and shape, so a test wired to the wrong operator fails
// here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] elementwise_mul [512x512]: PASS
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] elementwise_mul [4096x768]: PASS
